{"text":"And let us go back into the 1950s and think about what it was that motivated people to start this whole aid regime. It was post-World War II, Bretton Woods had been established, and it was on the back of the success of the Marshall Plan, where we had seen what is equivalent to about $100 billion being sent into Europe and used for reconstruction and development. So people were quite excited. They thought, gosh, if it worked in Europe, why should it not work in Africa? And I have to confess, if I had been a policymaker in the 1950s and 60s, I would have been a big supporter of aid, because conceptually it made sense. We know savings leads to investment, leads to growth, which is a simple economic identity. But if there's no saving, why don't we give them aid, which should lead to investment, which leads to growth, which should reduce poverty? It absolutely made sense. But here we are today, about 50 years later, and there has been over a trillion dollars of aid sent to Africa. That is about $100 for every man, woman and child on the planet of Earth today.","words":[{"text":"And","start":0.0,"end":1.08},{"text":"let","start":1.08,"end":1.94},{"text":"us","start":1.94,"end":2.12},{"text":"go","start":2.12,"end":2.48},{"text":"back","start":2.48,"end":2.78},{"text":"into","start":2.78,"end":3.0},{"text":"the","start":3.0,"end":3.2},{"text":"1950s","start":3.2,"end":4.2},{"text":"and","start":4.2,"end":4.34},{"text":"think","start":4.34,"end":4.56},{"text":"about","start":4.56,"end":4.86},{"text":"what","start":4.86,"end":5.18},{"text":"it","start":5.18,"end":5.34},{"text":"was","start":5.34,"end":5.66},{"text":"that","start":5.66,"end":6.32},{"text":"motivated","start":6.32,"end":6.98},{"text":"people","start":6.98,"end":7.42},{"text":"to","start":7.42,"end":7.62},{"text":"start","start":7.62,"end":7.9},{"text":"this","start":7.9,"end":8.08},{"text":"whole","start":8.08,"end":8.32},{"text":"aid","start":8.32,"end":8.52},{"text":"regime","start":8.52,"end":8.92,